<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Javier de Burgos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1778–1848</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Javier de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgos">Burgos</a> was a Spanish politician, writer and translator from Motril. As minister of development in 1833 he carried out the territorial division of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> into 49 provinces grouped in historical regions, which with few changes remains the basis of Spanish provinces today. He also translated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horace">Horace</a> and later served again as a minister under Isabella II.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/javier-de-burgos.jpg" alt="Javier de Burgos" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antonio María Esquivel · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Francisco_Javier_de_Burgos_(Ministerio_del_Interior).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
